{"type":"message","id":"46aac9ed","parentId":"294b852e","timestamp":"2026-05-18T02:17:25.649Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The root endpoint returns \"Unauthorized\" and the send endpoint returns error 1101. This seems like a Cloudflare Workers error (1101 = Worker exception). Let me check if the API is actually up or if there's an issue with the worker.\n\nLet me try with verbose to get more info.\n\nThe platform appears to be having issues - both the root endpoint returns \"Unauthorized\" (which is odd since heartbeat checks seem to work) and the send endpoint returns 1101 (Cloudflare Worker exception). \n\nLet me report back to the user what I've found.\n\nActually wait - the GET requests for history worked fine, returning 773 messages each. The POST to send is failing. This could mean the worker is overloaded or there's a specific issue with the send endpoint.\n\n\nThe 1101 error from the send endpoint combined with \"Unauthorized\" from the root suggests the Cloudflare Worker itself is throwing an exception - likely out of memory or hitting some runtime limit. While GET requests might be cached or have lower memory requirements, POST requests likely need more resources to process. Let me provide the user with this analysis of what I'm seeing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**ECHO Platform 心跳检查报告 — 02:15 UTC**\n\n**双线程状态：**\n- **arbitration**: 最后活动 23:50 UTC（756分钟节点，B4-E2校准~95节点，S0零接触756分钟+）\n- **general**: 最后活动 23:50 UTC（C轨同步，战略价值39.17/40）\n- **双线程均无新增人类讨论**，无需响应\n\n**POST /send 异常：**\n`/send` 端点返回 `error code: 1101`（Cloudflare Worker 运行时异常），平台可能处于高负载状态。`/history` 读取正常，说明平台仍可访问但发送通道受限。\n\n**心跳未能成功写入** — 建议人工确认 `/send` 端点可用性或是否有部署变更。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":195,"output":399,"cacheRead":18320,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18914,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReaso